# Spotify Web API owner credentials for `npm run music:fetch` (never commit .env.local).
# The refresh script loads .env.local automatically; CI can provide the same names as secrets.
#
# 1. Create a Spotify Developer app and register an exact loopback redirect URI,
#    e.g. http://127.0.0.1:8888/callback.
# 2. Authorize the owner account once with the `user-top-read` scope.
# 3. Exchange the authorization code for a refresh token and store the three values below.
#
# Spotify Development Mode rules changed in 2026. The owner account/app must satisfy the
# current Development Mode requirements; see the Spotify developer dashboard/docs if auth
# returns 403. The showcase needs only `user-top-read` and performs six API calls per refresh.
#
# For the scheduled GitHub Action, add these same names under repository Actions secrets:
#   SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID, SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET, SPOTIFY_REFRESH_TOKEN
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=
SPOTIFY_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# Optional: Spotify Soloist local-device integration.
# This key is NOT used by the public /rotation page or the Spotify Web API refresh.
# Keep it local. Do not commit it, paste it into chat, expose it to the browser, or add it
# to NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables. Soloist uses this key only to start its local Linux daemon.
SPOTIFY_SOLOIST_API_KEY=
SOLOIST_DEVICE_NAME=Sid Neural Net
SOLOIST_WS_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1:9090
